In $\triangle ABC$, the sides opposite to angles $A$, $B$, $C$ are $a$, $b$, $c$ respectively, and satisfy the vectors $\overrightarrow{m}=(\cos A,\cos B)$, $\overrightarrow{n}=(a,2c-b)$, and $\overrightarrow{m} \parallel \overrightarrow{n}$.
