Given an ellipse C: $$\frac {x^{2}}{a^{2}}$$ + $$\frac {y^{2}}{b^{2}}$$ = 1 (a > b > 0) with an eccentricity of $$\frac { \sqrt {2}}{2}$$, the length of the line segment obtained by intersecting the line y = 1 with the ellipse C is 2$$\sqrt {2}$$.
