In acute triangle $\triangle ABC$, the sides opposite to angles $A$, $B$, $C$ are $a$, $b$, $c$ respectively. Given that $a \neq b$, $c = \sqrt{3}$, and $\sqrt{3} \cos^2 A - \sqrt{3} \cos^2 B = \sin A \cos A - \sin B \cos B$.

