For the set $M$, define the function $f_M(x) = \begin{cases} -1, & x \in M \\ 1, & x \notin M \end{cases}$. For two sets $M$ and $N$, define the set $M \triangle N = \{x | f_M(x) \cdot f_N(x) = -1\}$. Given $A = \{2, 4, 6, 8, 10\}$ and $B = \{1, 2, 4, 8, 16\}$.

